Keep the extraction root as the boundary when extending cached paths.

Patch origin: in-house
Patch status: Solaris adaptation of the imported extraction-fd stack

Prerequisite: security-02-extraction-fds.patch and the subsequent
security-04-CVE-2026-18508.patch descriptor-cache adjustments.

When confinement is active, a cached subdirectory is not the confinement
root. For example, after caching a/ for a/file, resolving b/ relative to
that cache rejects a/b -> ../c even though c/ is under the extraction root.
Resolve the full parent from chdir_fd in this case, retaining all configured
openat2 restrictions. Keep the cache-extension shortcut for unconfined
operations and exact-parent cache hits.

--- a/src/misc.c
+++ b/src/misc.c
@@ -1303,10 +1303,13 @@
       *p = '\0';
 
       if (submatch && c->subdirlen < subdirlen
-	  && !ISSLASH (subdir[c->subdirlen]))
-	{
-	  /* The new directory is a subdirectory of the old,
-	     so open relative to FD rather than to chdir_fd.  */
+	  && !ISSLASH (subdir[c->subdirlen])
+	  && !open_searchdir_how.resolve)
+	{
+	  /* Without confinement, open relative to the cached directory.
+	     With confinement, resolve the full parent from chdir_fd below:
+	     a symlink can leave the cached directory while remaining
+	     beneath the extraction root.  */
 	  int subfd = open_subdir (fd, &subdir[c->subdirlen]);
 	  if (subfd < 0)
 	    {
